cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this, please cite it.
title: "Precedent poisoning: how one stale file changes what a coding agent writes"
authors:
  - family-names: Wade
    given-names: Paul
repository-code: "https://github.com/paul-wade/precedent-poisoning"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-11
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - static analysis
  - software engineering
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  A harness that holds a task fixed and varies the repository around it. Five
  tasks each ask an agent for a sibling of a file that already takes a
  shortcut, under three environments: the repository alone, a conventions
  file, and a lint gate that reads each edit before it lands. Ungated, the
  agent reproduced the shortcut in 20 of 25 trials. Trials that read no
  compliant example first did so in 17 of 18.
